{
  "title": "Go service: learning dashboard",
  "uid": "go-service-learning",
  "tags": ["go", "otel", "learning"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "editable": true,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus"
      },
      {
        "name": "job",
        "label": "Service (job)",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(go_info, job)",
          "refId": "job"
        },
        "includeAll": false
      },
      {
        "name": "instance",
        "label": "Instance",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(go_info{job=~\"$job\"}, instance)",
          "refId": "instance"
        },
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**Read top to bottom.** *Traffic* tells you **if** users are hurting. *Resources* and *Go runtime* tell you **why**. *Lifecycle* tells you if the process is stable and configured as you think.\n\n- **Counter** (`_total`, `_count`, `_bucket`): only goes up. Never graph it raw, wrap it in `rate(x[$__rate_interval])` to get *per second*.\n- **Gauge** (`go_goroutines`, `process_resident_memory_bytes`): a current value. Graph it raw; use `deriv()` for its trend, never `rate()`.\n- **Histogram** (`_bucket`): `histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(x_bucket[...])))` gives p99. Always `sum by (le)` before the quantile.\n- `$__rate_interval` is sized by Grafana to the scrape/export interval (60s here), so `rate()` always has at least two points.\n\nHover the **(i)** on each panel for what it means and what to look for. Click **Edit** to see and tweak the query.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Traffic (RED: rate, errors, duration)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Requests per second",
      "description": "**Rate** of the RED method. Counter `_count` of the latency histogram, wrapped in `rate()`.\n\nSplit by route and status code. Requests that match no route (404s) have no `http_route`, so they show only the code.\n\nLook for: sudden drops (callers can't reach you) or spikes (retry storms, a new client).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (http_route, http_response_status_code) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{http_route}} {{http_response_status_code}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Error ratio (5xx)",
      "description": "**Errors** of the RED method: 5xx responses / all responses. 4xx are the caller's fault, so they are excluded.\n\nEmpty means no 5xx at all, which is good. Look for: anything above your SLO budget, usually 0.1-1%.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\", http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "5xx ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Latency p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "**Duration** of the RED method, from histogram buckets. p50 is the typical request, p99 is the slowest 1%.\n\nThe handler sleeps 5ms, so expect p50 around 5-10ms. Quantiles are interpolated inside a bucket (5ms, 10ms, 25ms...), so they're estimates. Look for: p99 drifting away from p50, which usually means queueing or GC.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Resources",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 7,
      "title": "CPU (cores)",
      "description": "`rate(process_cpu_seconds_total)`: CPU seconds used per second, which equals cores in use. 0.25 = a quarter of one core.\n\nLook for: values near the container's CPU limit, which means throttling and higher latency.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(process_cpu_seconds_total{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Memory",
      "description": "**RSS** (`process_resident_memory_bytes`) is what the OS counts and what gets you OOM-killed. **Heap in use** is the part the Go runtime is actively using.\n\nRSS > heap because of stacks, runtime overhead and memory the GC freed but hasn't returned to the OS yet. Look for: RSS approaching the container memory limit, or a line that only goes up (leak).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "process_resident_memory_bytes{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "RSS {{instance}}"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "go_memstats_heap_inuse_bytes{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "heap in use {{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Allocation rate",
      "description": "`rate(go_memstats_alloc_bytes_total)`: bytes allocated per second. Not memory *held*, memory *churned*.\n\nHigh allocation rate = more GC work = more CPU. Look for: a jump after a deploy, which usually means a new hot path allocating per request.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(go_memstats_alloc_bytes_total{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Go runtime",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Goroutines",
      "description": "`go_goroutines`: a gauge. Under steady traffic it should be flat.\n\nLook for: a line that keeps climbing and never comes back down. That's a goroutine leak (a blocked channel, a missing context cancel, a request without a timeout).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "go_goroutines{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 12,
      "title": "GC pause (stop-the-world)",
      "description": "`go_gc_duration_seconds` is a summary: quantile=\"1\" is the worst recent pause, 0.5 the median. While paused, no goroutine runs, so every in-flight request waits.\n\nIn modern Go pauses are usually well under 1ms. Look for: pauses in the ms range lining up with p99 latency spikes.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "go_gc_duration_seconds{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\", quantile=\"1\"}",
          "legendFormat": "max {{instance}}"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "go_gc_duration_seconds{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\", quantile=\"0.5\"}",
          "legendFormat": "median {{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 13,
      "title": "GC cycles per second",
      "description": "`rate(go_gc_duration_seconds_count)`: how often the GC runs. It's driven by the allocation rate and GOGC/GOMEMLIMIT.\n\nLook for: GC running many times per second while memory is near GOMEMLIMIT. That's the GC fighting to stay under the limit and burning CPU.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(go_gc_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Lifecycle and config",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Uptime",
      "description": "`time() - process_start_time_seconds`. A small uptime you didn't expect means the process restarted.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "time() - process_start_time_seconds{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 16,
      "title": "Restarts (1h)",
      "description": "`changes(process_start_time_seconds[1h])`: the start time only changes when the process restarts. Anything above 0 without a deploy means crashes or OOM kills.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 4,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "changes(process_start_time_seconds{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h])",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 17,
      "title": "File descriptors used",
      "description": "`process_open_fds / process_max_fds`. Every socket (HTTP, Postgres, Redis, Kafka) is an FD. Reaching 100% means `too many open files` and new connections fail.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.6
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.8
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "process_open_fds{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"} / process_max_fds{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 18,
      "title": "GOMAXPROCS",
      "description": "`go_sched_gomaxprocs_threads`: how many OS threads run Go code at once. Since Go 1.25 it follows the container's CPU limit. If it shows the host's core count inside a limited container, you'll get throttling.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "go_sched_gomaxprocs_threads{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 19,
      "title": "GOMEMLIMIT",
      "description": "`go_gc_gomemlimit_bytes`: the soft memory limit the GC aims for. \"unlimited\" is the default. In a container, set it to ~90% of the memory limit so the GC works harder before the OOM killer steps in.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "range",
              "options": {
                "from": 9e18,
                "to": 1e19,
                "result": {
                  "text": "unlimited"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "go_gc_gomemlimit_bytes{job=~\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Go version",
      "description": "`go_info`: always 1, the information is in the `version` label. Useful to confirm a rollout actually changed the toolchain.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 34,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
